        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "21228c10-e6fe-5578-98b3-0f3d847a7757",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Fayard Nicholas, Harold Nicholas, Luci Martin, Bernard Edwards, Eugene Jackson, Sammy Warren\n- Groups: Nicholas Brothers, Our Gang\n- Songs: “My Feet Keep Dancing”\n- Films: “An All-Colored Vaudeville Show”, “Stormy Weather”, “The Pirate”, “Hard Four”\n- Roles: choreographer, dancer, actor, vocalist\n\nFacts:\n- Fayard Antonio Nicholas was born on October 20, 1914, and he was an American choreographer, dancer, and actor.\n- Fayard Nicholas and his younger brother Harold Nicholas formed the tap-dance duo the Nicholas Brothers.\n- The Nicholas Brothers starred in the MGM musical “An All-Colored Vaudeville Show” in 1935.\n- The Nicholas Brothers starred in the MGM musical “Stormy Weather” in 1943.\n- The Nicholas Brothers starred in the MGM musical “The Pirate” in 1948.\n- The song “My Feet Keep Dancing” features co-lead vocals by Luci Martin and Bernard Edwards.\n- The song “My Feet Keep Dancing” includes a tap dance solo by Fayard Nicholas, Eugene Jackson of Our Gang, and Sammy Warren.\n- The Nicholas Brothers starred in “Hard Four” in 2007.\n- Fayard Nicholas died on January 24, 2006.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "99b01936-a7da-5815-bcc8-b66417148f25",
        "text": "Page: My Feet Keep Dancing. Sentence: It features a co-lead vocal by Luci Martin and Bernard Edwards and a tap dance solo by Fayard Nicholas (of the Nicholas Brothers), Eugene Jackson (of Our Gang), and Sammy Warren.\nPage: Fayard Nicholas. Sentence: Fayard Antonio Nicholas (October 20, 1914 – January 24, 2006) was an American choreographer, dancer and actor.\nPage: Fayard Nicholas. Sentence: He and his younger brother Harold Nicholas made up the Nicholas Brothers tap-dance duo, who starred in the MGM musicals \"An All-Colored Vaudeville Show\" (1935), \"Stormy Weather\" (1943), \"The Pirate\" (1948), and \"Hard Four\" (2007).",
